<http://clinicaltrials.gov/ctgo#Condition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "As CTGO is used as a data scheme for the clinical trial registry at clinical trials.gov, this class can be understood as a medical condition class. Still, there is no definition, no comment and no expressive superclass or logical axiom. The ontology contains several class hierarchy instead of serological hierarchy confusion. E.g. Intervention study is a subclass of design. At best, part of the intervention study is the intervention design but the study itself is not the design. The ontology contains several class hierarchy instead of mereological hierarchy confusions. E.g. Intervention study is a subclass of design. At best, part of the intervention study is the intervention design but the study itself is not the design." .
