<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HINO_0015722> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "Is_a ino:human molecular pathway is_a ino:pathway is_a ino:interaction_network is a bfo:process. Thus, disease is a process with probably proteins as participant. Hence, ogms:disease and ino:disease are not equivalent although both are OBO ontologies. In this application-specific scope of disease as a pathway the definition seems sound but leaves the clinical view of disease totally untouched and unreusable for this use case." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HINO_0015722> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#reality_vs_classification> "biological_state" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HINO_0015722> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#retrieved_at_by_database> "BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:06:55-04:00" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HINO_0015722> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "is_a ino:human molecular pathway is_a ino:pathway is_a ino:interaction_network is a bfo:process. Thus, disease is a process with probably proteins as participant. Hence, ogms:disease and ino:disease are not equivalent although both are OBO ontologies. In this very narrow scope of disease as a pathway the definition seems sound but leaves the clinical view of disease totally untouched and unreusable for this use case." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HINO_0015722> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_date> "2026-07-06" .
