<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IDOMAL_0001241> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "With symp:symptom is_a idomal:condition of human host is_a idomal:condition and also idomal:infectious disease is_a bfo:disposition, condition here does not mean a synonym for disease but the phenotype of a disease. Very unusual position of symptom under realizable entity although symptom is seen as a process by other BFO abiding ontologists. (Modeling Biomedical Burdens in Basic Formal Ontology, Paul Smart, Nic Fair and Michael Boniface, 2024)." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IDOMAL_0001241> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#retrieved_at_by_database> "BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:16:24-04:00; BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:16:29-04:00" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IDOMAL_0001241> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "With symp:symptom is_a idomal:condition of human host is_a idomal:condition and also  idomal:infectious disease is_a bfo:disposition,  condition here doesn't mean a synonym for disease but the phenotype of a disease.  |  Very strange position of symptom under realizable entity although symptom is seen as a process by other BFO abiding ontologists. (Modeling Biomedical Burdens in Basic Formal Ontology,  Paul Smart, Nic Fair and Michael Boniface, 2024)" .
