<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MPATH_0> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "Mpath:pathological entity is_a mpath:pathological phenotype observation. Grandchild is for example neoplasm is_a pathological anatomical entity is_a pathological entity. Thus, MAPTH seems not like an ontology in a sense of modelling our shared conceptualisation of reality but rather an endeavour to group certain observations into buckets. Because, a neoplasm is not an observation but the observation entity is created when observing a neoplasm. There is no definition of pathological." .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MPATH_0> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#reality_vs_classification> "nosological_category" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MPATH_0> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#retrieved_at_by_database> "BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:18:58-04:00; BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:19:03-04:00; BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:19:08-04:00" .
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MPATH_0> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "mpath:pathological entity is_a mpath:pathological phenotype observation. Grandchild is for example neoplasm is_a pathological anatomical entity is_a pathological entity. Thus, MAPTH seems not like an ontology in a sense of modelling our shared conceptualisation of reality but rather an endeavour to group certain observations into buckets. Because clearly, a neoplasm isn't an observation but the observation entity is created when observing a neoplasm. There is no definition of pathological." .
