<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000102> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#comment_values_json> "[\"At the scale of organism (as opposed to the cellular scale or the population scale), an injury is typically the result of a catastrophic event. Consider the implications of making 'injury' a subtype of 'disorder'.; At the scale of organism (as opposed to the cellular scale or the population scale), an injury is typically the result of a catastrophic event. Consider the implications of making 'injury' a subtype of 'disorder'. Note: Adopted subtype of disorder, and injury can occur at the scale of organism down to cellular level.\"]" .
