<http://www.projecthalo.com/aura#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "Very broad definition that could be: the abnormal condition of low oxygen because of very high altitude during skydiving causing hypoxemia. Low oxygen is not a disease. The class itself is not modelled very ontologically. Subclass of aura:Disease is aura:Genetic_disorder next to aura:Cancer. Aura:Genetic_disorder has as subclass aura:Gap_in_segmentation which is a mutation in common sense. Its nephew aura:Huntington's-Disease is a disease in common sense. The parent aura:Intangible-Entity would need further explanation. Because aura:Cancer which is an aura:Disease and thus a aura:IntangibleEntity is very tangible in common understanding. Apart from that, several wrong is_a relationships: Morphology is_a Biology is_an Inquiry is_an Event as well as State is_an Event. No definition is given ever, so in theory this model could be correct but must denote entities with very different names or have very different definitions than every other top ontology." .
<http://www.projecthalo.com/aura#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#reality_vs_classification> "biological_state" .
<http://www.projecthalo.com/aura#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#retrieved_at_by_database> "BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:06:55-04:00" .
<http://www.projecthalo.com/aura#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "Very broad definition that could be: the abnormal condition of low oxygen because of very high altitude during skydiving causing hypoxemia. Low oxygen clearly isn't a disease. The class itself isn't modelled very ontologically. Subclass of aura:Disease is aura:Genetic_disorder next to aura:Cancer. aura:Genetic_disorder has as subclass aura:Gap_in_segmentation which is a mutation in common sense. Its nephew aura:Huntington's-Disease is a disease in common sense. The parent aura:Intangible-Entity would need further explanation. Because aura:Cancer which is an aura:Disease and thus a aura:IntangibleEntity is very tangible in common understanding. Apart from that, several wrong is_a relationships: Morphology is_a Biology is_an Inquiry is_an Event as well as State is_an Event. No definition is given ever, so in theory this model could be correct but must denote entities with very different names or have very different definitions than every other top ontology." .
