<http://www.semanticweb.org/ontologies/epo.owl#HealthCondition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#retrieved_at_by_database> "BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:18:23-04:00" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ontologies/epo.owl#HealthCondition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "Clear Menelas top-grounding. The class does not read as a disease entity itself, but as a clinical/phenotypic manifestation or diagnostic interpretation of an underlying internal state. However, internal state is modeled as a sibling rather than a superclass or defining substrate, and both health condition and internal state are placed under maternal state. This makes the modelling highly scope-bound to early pregnancy/maternal context, with no clear built-in reusability as a general disease or health-condition class." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/ontologies/epo.owl#HealthCondition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_date> "2026-07-06" .
