<http://www.semanticweb.org/parracarlos/ontologies/2019/3/untitled-ontology-31#Condition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_comment_status> "approved" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/parracarlos/ontologies/2019/3/untitled-ontology-31#Condition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "Application-specific definition as a drug adherence influencing factor, no other parent class. IRI is \"untitled ontology\". Very broad term used for application-specific use case. No philosophical grounding of the term. Still health related. Crisp/graded borderline: weak gradedness in data candidate; kept as silent because annotation mentions 'severity' in definition, but does not show that severity/stage is modelled as data. Evidence: definition[severity]: whether most or all of the time he or she is in bed). The presence of symptoms and their severity, as well as the progression of symptoms and the disease itself, are also factors addressed here. In addition, if the patient has a condition of drug addiction, comorbidity or doe. Comments[severity]: whether most or all of the time he or she is in bed). The presence of symptoms and their severity, as well as the progression of symptoms and the disease itself, are also factors addressed here. In addition, if the patient has a condition of drug addiction, comorbidity or doe." .
