<http://www.semanticweb.org/zchero/ontologies/2023/11/SepsisOntology#Syndrome> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#preferred_label> "Syndrome" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/zchero/ontologies/2023/11/SepsisOntology#Syndrome> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_comment_status> "approved" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/zchero/ontologies/2023/11/SepsisOntology#Syndrome> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "Syndrome as subclass of inflammation has an application-specific scope. On the other hand, it is not a true class hierarchy with Etiology is_a Sepsis. Sepsis might have an identifiable reason for its development which you could summarise as Etiology but it is not one. The definition is only clinical and not ontological." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/zchero/ontologies/2023/11/SepsisOntology#Syndrome> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#reality_vs_classification> "conflated" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/zchero/ontologies/2023/11/SepsisOntology#Syndrome> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#retrieved_at_by_database> "BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:17:03-04:00" .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/zchero/ontologies/2023/11/SepsisOntology#Syndrome> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "Syndrome as subclass of inflammation has obviously a very narrow scope. On the other hand, it isn't a true class hierarchy with Etiology is_a Sepsis. Clearly, sepsis might have an identifiable reason for its development which you could summarise as Etiology but it isn't one. The definition is only clinical and not ontological." .
<http://www.semanticweb.org/zchero/ontologies/2023/11/SepsisOntology#Syndrome> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_date> "2026-07-09" .
