<https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/Condition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "A medical Condition is meant but as state without mentioning what a state is and no reference to other aspects of a condition like the dispositional or procedural aspect. Bto:Subclass of Condition is bto:Comorbidity defined as the existence of two processes. A state and a process seem mutually exclusive. A sibling class is bro:\"Disease, Disorder or Finding\" which seems very much non-ontological. In addition to the fact that condition is just subclass of owl:Thing, this class seems ill-defined." .
<https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/Condition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#reality_vs_classification> "unclear" .
<https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/Condition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#retrieved_at_by_database> "BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:15:56-04:00" .
<https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/Condition> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "Clearly a medical Condition is meant but as state without mentioning what a state is and no reference to other aspects of a condition like the dispositional or procedural aspect.  |  bto:Subclass of Condition is bto:Comorbidity defined as the existence of two processes. A state and a process seem mutually exclusive. A sibling class is bro:\"Disease, Disorder or Finding\" which seems very much non-ontological. In addition to the fact that condition is just subclass of owl:thng, this class seems ill-defined." .
