<https://w3id.org/codo#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "Oddly, three definitions are pasted from MSH, NCI and PSY. Even more oddly, codo:Disorder is_a Pathological state is_a Condition as well as Disorder is_a Condition . Finally, this definition is too weak to exclude \"hypoxemia from being in very high altitude\" which is easily reversible and can't be seen as a disease. Spoken from the definition, although pathological state seems similar to Kantian \"state\", this entity appears like not conveying any ontological meaning Crisp/graded borderline: weak crisp candidate; kept as silent because criteria-like phrase in definition ('characteristic set'), but no explicit necessary/sufficient or vagueness handling. Evidence: definition[characteristic set]: A definite pathologic process with a characteristic set of signs and symptoms. It may affect the whole body or any of its parts, and its etiology, pathology, and prognosis may be known or unknown. (MSH); Conceptually broad term referri | comments[characteristic set]: festyle choices, or a combination of these factors.; A definite pathologic process with a characteristic set of signs and symptoms. It may affect the whole body or any of its parts, and its etiology, pathology, and prognosis may be known or unknown. (MSH); Conceptually broad term referri" .
