<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#comment_quality> "partial" .
<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#comment_values_json> "[\"A definite pathologic process with a characteristic set of signs and symptoms. It may affect the whole body or any of its parts, and its etiology, pathology, and prognosis may be known or unknown. (MSH); UMLS CUI: C0012634; Conceptually broad term referring primarily to physical illness. Also used when particular disorders are not specified. Use a more specific term if possible. For general discussions of health impairment consider also the term HEALTH. (PSY); Any abnormal condition of the body or mind that causes discomfort, dysfunction, or distress to the person affected or those in contact with the person. The term is often used broadly to include injuries, disabilities, syndromes, symptoms, deviant behaviors, and atypical variations of structure and function. (NCI)\"]" .
<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#crisp_vs_graded> "silent" .
<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#definition_quality> "partial" .
<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#definition_values_json> "[\"Conceptually broad term referring primarily to physical illness. Also used when particular disorders are not specified. Use a more specific term if possible. For general discussions of health impairment consider also the term HEALTH. (PSY); Any abnormal condition of the body or mind that causes discomfort, dysfunction, or distress to the person affected or those in contact with the person. The term is often used broadly to include injuries, disabilities, syndromes, symptoms, deviant behaviors, and atypical variations of structure and function. (NCI); A definite pathologic process with a characteristic set of signs and symptoms. It may affect the whole body or any of its parts, and its etiology, pathology, and prognosis may be known or unknown. (MSH); UMLS CUI: C0012634\"]" .
<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#discovery_tier> "primary_exact_label" .
