<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "Subclass of process but placed next to ogms:disease as sibling which is a disposition. The annotation combines three source definitions without reconciliation. Crisp/graded borderline: weak crisp candidate; kept as silent because criteria-like phrase in definition ('characteristic set'), but no explicit necessary/sufficient or vagueness handling. Evidence: definition[characteristic set]: typical variations of structure and function. (NCI); A definite pathologic process with a characteristic set of signs and symptoms. It may affect the whole body or any of its parts, and its etiology, pathology, and prognosis may be known or unknown. (MSH); UMLS CUI: C0012634. Comments[characteristic set]: A definite pathologic process with a characteristic set of signs and symptoms. It may affect the whole body or any of its parts, and its etiology, pathology, and prognosis may be known or unknown. (MSH); UMLS CUI: C0012634; Conceptuall." .
<https://w3id.org/opencare#Disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#reality_vs_classification> "biological_state" .
