<urn:agi-folder:disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#publication_review_comment_proposed> "Bpt:Disease as a subclass of bpt:Pathway focusses on molecular interactions rather than clinical presentation. All bpt:Pathway leafs are proper process-like pathways. But, the classes in between are typically perceived as continuants. Full example: bpt:CCR5 Signaling in Macrophages is_a bpt:blood is_a bpt:Tissues is_a bpt: Anatomy index is_an Index is_a Pathways. Although denoted as taxonomy, the hierarchy contains false or at least unusual is_a relationships. 1. Bpt:Wilson's Disease is_a bpt:Wilson's disease. 2. Bpt:Oxidative Stress in vitiligo is_a bpt:Vitiligo." .
