<urn:agi-folder:disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#retrieved_at_by_database> "BioPortal: 2026-06-29T20:06:55-04:00" .
<urn:agi-folder:disease> <urn:uuid:8f96cf34-53c2-48d2-88c5-96d07704fcf7#review_comment> "bpt:Disease as a subclass of bpt:Pathway focusses on molecular interactions rather than clinical presentation. All bpt:Pathway leafs are proper process-like pathways. But, the classes in between are typically perceived as continuants. Full example: bpt:CCR5 Signaling in Macrophages is_a bpt:blood is_a bpt:Tissues is_a bpt: Anatomy index is_an Index is_a Pathways.  |  although denoted as taxonomy, the hierarchy contains false or at least strange is_a relationships.  1. bpt:Wilson's Disease is_a bpt:Wilson's disease.   2. bpt:Oxidative Stress in vitiligo is_a bpt:Vitiligo" .
